08","agent_session":"sase-1ra.1","agent_session_role":"plan","bead_id":"sase-1ra.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1ra[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Next-ten task beads: honest update-skew failures, reboot recovery, [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]and the false-red test backlog[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The ten task beads ranked by the 2026-11-04 next-ten research [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]report are fixed, verified, and closed, together with the three [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]beads the report attached to them (sase-1i6, sase-1jd, sase-12u). [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]None of this work collides with the live Agent Hijack (sase-1qz), [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]publication (sase-1r8), or v0.19.0 release (sase-1r2) epics.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]12[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]next_ten_task_beads.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/next_ten_task_beads.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1ra[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1ra/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]-p accepts a project's display name, alias, or key (sase-zo)[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]project_names[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]project_names: canonicalize -p/--project through the project registry in[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolve_project_context, list candidates on ambiguity, and add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]display-name-differs-from-key regressions (sase-zo).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A failed $EDITOR never deletes the typed draft (sase-1ce)[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]editor_drafts[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]editor_drafts: on a non-zero editor exit or read failure, keep and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]recover changed prompt and workflow-YAML drafts instead of unlinking [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]them (sase-1ce).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pytest isolation: scrub SASE_MODEL_OVERRIDE and O(1) per-test [bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]homes (sase-1q3, sase-1qe)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]pytest_env[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pytest_env: add SASE_MODEL_OVERRIDE to the autouse env scrub and replace[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the per-test mktemp home allocation with a per-worker parent plus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mkdtemp, both in tests/_conftest_environment.py (sase-1q3, sase-1qe).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]FIFO fairness for pytest worker-token waiters (sase-1pw)[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]token_fifo[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pytest_env[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]token_fifo: give WorkerTokenLease waiters cross-process FIFO arrival [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tickets with bounded backfill and dead-waiter reclamation, proven by a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fake-clock starvation test (sase-1pw).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]False-red batch: cold keymap test, MRU provider pruning, [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]AF_UNIX path length (sase-1qu, sase-172, sase-1i6)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]false_red[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]false_red: fix three tests that fail deterministically when run cold or [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]alone, repairing product behavior where the root cause is a product bug [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](sase-1qu, sase-172, sase-1i6).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Command-line panel pilot trio passes on apollo (sase-1al)[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel_pilot[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel_pilot: remove the grammar-load race from the three [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]test_panel_shell_pilot.py nodes without raising timeouts, and verify 20x[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]serial plus 3x -n 8 on apollo (sase-1al).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Signature-skew TypeErrors are classified and explained as [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]update skew (sase-1r4, Python half)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]skew_label[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]skew_label: teach runner_failure_facts and code_swap_explanation the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]signature-mismatch TypeError shapes, gated on a proven code-identity [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]move, without silencing failure notifications (sase-1r4 part 1).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Orphaned staged monitors settle and crashed members stay [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]listed (sase-1r4, zombie half)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]staged_zombie[dim] · [dim][/dim]after skew_label[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]staged_zombie: settle a staged monitor whose adopter died into a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]terminal held or failed state within one reconcile pass, and keep the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]crashed member row visible in sase agent list -a (sase-1r4 part 2).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [